# Draft 3 round-2 dispositions

Only the reviews’ final sections are used. Each finding was checked against docs/decisions.md, its authoritative core_rows.json notes, the relevant legacy spec and A1_BOUNDARIES.md. agy had no repo access; its claims below were checked independently. Question numbers retain draft-2 identities; 12 and 13 are removed. No owner decision is made by this proposal.

- Codex C2/Q12 — accepted: OD106, ARITH-10 and the no-hidden-traps decision already fix "'`try_convert -> Result<T, OutOfRange>`; restore it and remove Q12. CHANGES_v2’s agy C2 and unflagged conversion-error dispositions wrongly reopened it.
- Codex C1/Q13 — partly accepted: restore Q3.8’s zero-sized index order; reject deferral of other sequence/map orders because Q2.3 decides them too. CHANGES_v2’s Kimi C1, agy C1 and unflagged destruction-order dispositions were wrong.
- Codex P4/Q17 — accepted: native addresses/padding cannot be forced to match Core’s oracle; check each native trace against an allowed Core execution, preserving raw observations and exact equality for deterministic behavior. Correct CHANGES_v2’s agy C8/S3 “matched choices” implication.
- Codex C4/C8 assessment — accepted: Q3.11 supports structured values plus a raw store joined by Rep; specify materialized reads, writes and invalidation without claiming preservation proved.
- Codex certificates/maximal behavior assessment — partly accepted: compiler-execution certificates are supported, but Q9.9 and A1 still require infinite-prefix adequacy and compatible finite-prefix refinement; add them despite Codex finding no further blocker.
- Kimi Q12 — accepted: same OD106/ARITH-10 correction; ConversionError would change a decided API.
- Kimi Q13 — accepted: Q2.3 decides sequence and OrderedMap orders; preserve Heap and present-payload cases from its row note too. Only implementation waits.
- Kimi C8/section 3 — accepted: Q9.9 and A1’s “Fuel and divergence”/“Behaviour refinement” require compatible prefix limits for silent divergence and infinite interaction, plus finite target-prefix correspondence.
- Kimi C3 — accepted: Q4.5 decides only StaticStr’s explicit FFI adapter; Q3.1–Q3.4/Q4.6–Q4.7 decide view semantics, not physical layout. Common shared/mutable layout is marked proposed and concrete layout deferred.
- Kimi revision register — accepted: add Q3.10’s `base + size ≤ 2''^64−1` and the dependent u64 contracts in Q1.11/Q2.4/Q4.6 under Q3.5; narrower representation cannot silently revise them.
- agy prior rejections — accepted: rechecking INFOFLOW, Q9.11/OD144 and SPARK supports CHANGES_v2’s rejection of optional CT, reopened release metadata and reopened ensures timing.
- agy C3/Q5 niche machinery — accepted: make niche-decoding laws conditional on adoption; tagged-only foundations require no niche machinery.
- agy C1/C9 consumed parameters — partly accepted: clarify consumed/scope-cleaned parameters are invisible. Reject implied old-style contract access: Q9.11’s notes, OD117 and CON-3 explicitly forbid snapshots; entry-to-exit relations are Lean theorems. This also corrects the task’s attribution of old-style access to decided rows.
- agy hybrid materialization trigger — accepted: proposed C4 completion keeps safe loans structured; raw address-taking/expose/foreign address passing materializes bytes, reusing existing mappings. Q3.11 permits this formalization but does not decide these details.
- agy hybrid typed-write padding — accepted: proposed typed stores update active bytes/fragments and preserve padding and inactive storage, including initialization state; no fresh padding query on typed rewrite. Lowerings must prove this rule.
- agy hybrid safe reads — accepted: materialized typed reads apply partial Rep decoding themselves; invalid initialization/representation/permissions yield stuckness, consistent with Q6.7 and A1, never invented values.
- agy oracle determinism — partly accepted: pure history/site/occurrence queries make Core evaluation deterministic; reject mandatory native query synchronization, which neither Q9.9 nor native execution provides. P4 uses per-run allowed-observation witnesses.
- agy simulation direction — partly accepted: add forward simulation plus target determinism, finite stuttering and receptiveness/progress hypotheses, or direct backward refinement. Reject the premise that every Concrete loop/recursion terminates: Q2.6 and Q9.9 retain partial correctness/divergence.
- agy UTF-8 citation — accepted: cite TYPE-3/Q4.6–Q4.7 for text validity/ranges and separate text failure mapping from scalar ArithmeticError.
- agy startup-code citation — accepted as verification: Q7.10 explicitly fixes missing-grant refusal 125 and trap exit 134; C6’s authority includes Q7.1–Q7.11. The runtime decision fixes the line format; no correction to 125 itself is needed.

## Owner-question verdicts

Each line records the round-2 recommendation as well as any resulting change; agreement is not owner approval.
